{"content":"# ⚠️ **IMPORTANT: `toString().contains(...)` assertions are vacuous**

```dart
expect(
  agent.state.messages.map((m) => m.toString().contains('old big')),
  everyElement(isFalse),
);
```

`Message`/`UserMessage`/`AssistantMessage` do not override `toString()` (checked `lib/src/types.dart` and `lib/src/context.dart`), so `m.toString()` renders `Instance of 'UserMessage'` — the assertion evaluates `contains` on a constant string and **can never fail, regardless of message content**. The same pattern repeats at the `'yyyy'` assertion in the structured-projection test. The `reason` text ("no summary+source double-count") claims coverage these lines cannot provide.

Assert on the real content instead, e.g.:

```dart
String textOf(Message m) => switch (m) {
  final UserMessage u => u.content is String ? u.content as String : '',
  final AssistantMessage a => a.content
      .whereType<TextContent>()
      .map((t) => t.text)
      .join(),
